  "description": "A managed MIL-STD-188-110D Appendix D 3 kHz serial-tone HF modem for .NET: waveforms WN0 to WN8 and WN13 (Walsh, BPSK, QPSK, 8PSK, 16QAM), the autobaud preamble with waveform identification, mini-probe framing, the scrambler, the K7 and K9 convolutional codes with Table D-L puncturing and tail-biting soft decoding, the short and long block interleavers, and a probe-trained decision-feedback equaliser with iterative BCJR turbo equalisation. Bits in, 9600 Hz audio out on an 1800 Hz sub-carrier, and back. Implemented spec-first and validated against the standard's own performance masks in simulation. Extracted from the pdn-soundmodem packet-radio modem.",
